# SEGRAYTRACE on e5hex1: the chief-ray slot re-aimed at segment 3's reference point and traced
# surface by surface to the focal plane (cmdref: Ray Tracing).  The segment leg lands ON Seg3
# (element 3) and the next leg goes to m2 (element 8).  (The deck's "flat.txt does not exist"
# lines are the fixture's missing grid file, declined by name -- pre-existing, not this command.)
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/e5hex1.in
segraytrace
3
7
0
# EXPECT: Enter segment number \(0=quit\)
# EXPECT: to Element\s+3 \(Seg3\s*\):[\s\S]*?Segment Length=\s+2\.23216815163573D\+04
# EXPECT: from Element\s+3 \(Seg3\s*\) to Element\s+8 \(m2\s*\):[\s\S]*?Segment Length=\s+2\.18180921532551D\+04
# EXPECT: Index\(i\)=\s+1\.450415713D\+00
# EXPECT: to Element\s+13
# A second segment in the same command prints too (CTRACE clears ifRayPrint on return; the
# handler set it once, before its loop, so segment 7 traced silently -- B.2 2026-10-17):
# EXPECT: from Element\s+0 \(InputRay\s*\) to Element\s+7 \(Seg7\s*\):[\s\S]*?Segment Length=\s+2\.20310020757986D\+04
# EXPECT: from Element\s+7 \(Seg7\s*\) to Element\s+8 \(m2\s*\):[\s\S]*?Direction=\s+-1\.03208762760953D-01 -2\.48028939046969D-01 -9\.63239117085985D-01
# EXPECT-NOT: is not a Segment
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
